{\rtf1\ansi
# Display-Scenarios.rtf
# ---------------------
#     Used by: On2it-WinFixIT-Scenarios.ps1
#    Location: Root of first USB partition
# Maintainers: Edit with care. Do not remove section headers or tags.
#   End-users: This file is for reference only.  It is non-editable.
#
# To launch system run:
#              RUN - On2it-WinFixIT.bat
# in the Root of this USB. It will then display the text in the sections below, dependant
# upon where you run it from.
#
#These sections actually supply the text to On2it-WinFixIT-CompatibilityChecker.ps1 in the colours shown.
#
[DISPLAY WHEN - First Opened]
$C ==================================================================================================${Reset}
$Y                                On2it-WinFixIT${W} - INTRODUCTION
$C ==================================================================================================${Reset}
 On2it-WinFixIT operates in these main phases:

$Y CHECK Compatibility$Rst checks the ability of your PC to run Windows 11,
    whether it has an OS loaded or not.

 It advises you whether your machine is capable of a:  
   -$W FULL Install$Rst if it is fully compatible, and passes all the tests.
   -$W BYPASS Install$Rst if your hardware is capable of running Windows 11, 
     but does not have all the security features that Microsoft likes to insist on. 
     This enables you to still install Windows 11 on older but capable machines. 

$Y INSTALL Windows$Rst then gives you the choice of your available options.

$W Once Windows is installed on your PC$Rst, whether installed from this USB or not, 
 you will also be able to:

$Y      DEBLOAT Windows 11$Rst itself, from much of the software that Microsoft insists on installing  
          along with Windows 11.  You can either accept all of our default advice, or since you 
          will receive$W FULL advice on each option$Rst, you can choose options that are right for$W YOU$Rst.  

$Y      OPEN Library$Rst to:
$W        - INSTALL$Rst Apps pre-loaded by us or ones you’ve added yourself,
$W        - READ$Rst Reference material — both off-line and on-line, 
$W        - USE$Rst Utilities and Downloadable Software, 
$W        - ADD$Rst your own Apps, Menus and Options, simply by adding files and folders to the USB. 
     
$Y      READ User Manual$Rst – if you want to.  But since the whole system explains itself as you progress, 
          you really shouldn't need to.  It's there if you need it.

[CLEAR] $Y Press ANY Key to continue...

[DISPLAY WHEN - MAIN MENU Required]
$C ==================================================================================================${Reset}
$Y                                On2it-WinFixIT${Reset} -$W MAIN MENU
$C ==================================================================================================${Reset}

 Because you started On2it-WinFixIT from within Windows, ALL options are available.
 You can:

$Y CHECK Compatibility$Rst
      If you are unsure whether this machine can run Windows 11, start here.
      The Compatibility Checker compares PROCESSOR, MEMORY, STORAGE and FIRMWARE
      against Microsoft’s requirements and produces a printable report.

$Y INSTALL Windows 11$Rst
      Choose either:
$W        - FULL Install$Rst  Uses Windows 11 enhanced security features.
$W        - BYPASS Install$Rst  Skips Microsoft's requirements.
      You do not need to run CHECK Compatibility first, but the checker provides
      fuller guidance if you do.

$Y DEBLOAT Windows 11$W - works on any already installed copy. $Rst
      Remove or restore optional components and privacy tweaks.  

$Y OPEN Library$Rst
      A multi-level, user-editable and infinitely-extensible
$W      Dynamic Menu System$Rst driven entirely by the files and folders on the USB.

      These enable you to:
$W        - INSTALL$Rst Microsoft Office, WinFixIT and any other Application already on the USB.
$W        - DOWNLOAD$Rst and/or Install other Applications, Utilities and Software tools,
$W        - EXPLORE$Rst Artificial Intelligence and other operating systems,
$W        - READ$Rst on-line and off-line reference materials,
$W        - UPDATE$Rst the Library itself. 😊

      At the last count there were 60 Menus containing 225 Options.
      Since these are ALL editable: you can modify, add, remove, or reorganise them yourself.
      So, your count may well vary. For full details see User Manual.

$Y READ User Manual$Rst
      The USB contains a WinFixIT - User Manual.pdf with screenshots and guidance.
      It is optional but useful for unfamiliar users.

[PROMPT] $Y CLICK an OPTION, or Enter (CHECK / INSTALL / DEBLOAT / OPEN / READ / exit)
===============================================================================================================


[DISPLAY WHEN - Booted from USB with a choice already made in Windows] 
$C ==================================================================================================${Reset}
$Y                 On2it-WinFixIT${Reset} - Compatibility Check ALREADY COMPLETED in Windows
$C ==================================================================================================${Reset}
$Y Congratulations $Rst - You have successfully re-booted from the USB

 When you ran the Windows11-CompatibilityChecker in Windows, you had the options of:
   - FULL Install,
   - BYPASS Install.
 You chose a$W <Option Selected> Install${Reset}.  

[PROMPT] Do you wish to proceed with a ${Y}<Option Selected> Install?
[PROMPT] Would you prefer to proceed with a ${Y}<Other Option> Install?
=================================================================================================================


[DISPLAY WHEN - Booted from USB with no prior choice in Windows]
$C=====================================================================================================${Reset}
$Y                 On2it-WinFixIT${Reset} - WITHOUT a Compatibility Check in Windows
$C=====================================================================================================${Reset}
You have booted from the USB, whilst you have an installation of Windows on your PC, without 
first having run the Windows11 Compatibility Checker under Windows - or NOT made a choice, if you did.

Only if the Compatibility Checker has the services of a full operating system, can it produce 
fully comprehensive results.  

If you run it from the Windows Installation environment, WinPE, which is all that is available
when you boot from a USB, the Checker will NOT be able to produce fully comprehensive results. 
 
You are strongly advised therefore to NOT run the Windows11-Compatibility Checker right NOW.  
You should:
   - Abandon this run.
   - Restart Windows on your PC, and  
   - Re-run On2it-WinFixIT.bat on the USB, from Windows.

[PROMPT]$YWould you prefer to run the Compatibility Checker from Windows?${Reset}
[PROMPT]$CYou realise, that if you run the Compatibility Checker right NOW, it WILL produce 
inconclusive results.  So, you will ALWAYS be advised to run a$Y 'BYPASS Install'$C - to be safe.  

If you want to be really sure whether your machine will be able to take a$Y 'FULL Install'$C 
of Windows, you should answer "N" to the next question.${Reset}

$Y Are you ABSOLUTELY SURE you want to run the Compatibility Checker NOW?
=============================================================================================


[DISPLAY WHEN - Booted from USB with no Windows on PC]
$C=====================================================================================================${Reset}
$Y                 On2it-WinFixIT${Reset} - WITHOUT a Windows Installation on the PC
$C=====================================================================================================${Reset}
You have booted from the USB, WITHOUT a Windows installation on your PC.  
So let's get it done.  You will be able to:

$Y CHECK Compatibility$Rst of your PC
      If you are unsure whether this machine can run Windows 11, do this first.
      The Compatibility Checker compares PROCESSOR, MEMORY, STORAGE and FIRMWARE
      against Microsoft’s requirements and produces a printable report.

     $W WinPE${Reset},$W Win${Reset}dows$W P${Reset}reinstallation$W E${Reset}nvironment, is all that can be run from a USB. 
      However, it does not have all the functionality of a fully installed version of Windows.  
      So, it will not be able to do all the checks that can be done from Windows itself.  
      Nevertheless, you will get an assessment of the capability of your machine to run Windows 11.

$Y INSTALL Windows 11$Rst
      Whether you CHECK Compatibility first, or not, you will be able to do either a:
$W        - FULL Install$Rst   Using Windows 11 enhanced security features, or a
$W        - BYPASS Install$Rst Skipping Microsoft's requirements.
      But it provides fuller guidance if you need it.

[PROMPT]Do you want to$Y CHECK Compatibility${Reset} first ?
[PROMPT]Do you want to$Y INSTALL Windows 11${Reset} ?
=============================================================================================
}